note SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
note Allen's look, part 1: the drawing kit. Handwritten Omega port of native/kernel/ui/paint.h and
note paint.c (aienux 4b24df65): integer sine, arctangent, exp(-x), log2, hash noise, light-weighted
note colour blending through the sky's transfer tables, and the glow, thread, rounded-rectangle and
note letter shapes. Every function gives the same integers as the C kit; tests/look-paint.om compares
note them value for value against the C harness. Needs font-data.om and font.om before it (afsqrt,
note afglyph) and pkinit once before any other call.
note Shared memory (declared here, used by every look-* module):
note Lg: 0 screen width, 1 height, 2 k (1/256 px per design px of a 1920x1080 design), 3 sky centre x,
note 4 sky centre y, 5..8 the clip rectangle x,y,w,h every shape is held inside (pkclip sets it),
note 9 the rounded rectangle's radius for pksdrrect, 10..15 PAINT scratch (unused so far).
note Nfrm: the frame being drawn, one packed RGB word (R<<16|G<<8|B) per pixel, rows Lg[0] apart.
note Nsky: the sky as it was made at startup, the same layout.
note Slin: ck_sky_lin, sRGB byte -> linear light Q15. Ssrgb: ck_sky_srgb16, light>>3 -> sRGB x16.
note Both are filled by pkinit from Plin/Psrgb, the exact values of sky_data.c.
note Pa: the argument block for calls with more than six values. pkthread reads Pa[0] = width in
note 16ths of a pixel, Pa[1] = a0, Pa[2] = a1 (its sixth value a01 is ignored; pass 0). pkletter's
note face is the font's own state (afinit before use). Ps is PAINT's private scratch.
note Signatures (same integers as the C): pksin/pkcos a (turns/65536) -> Q14; pkatan2 y x -> 0..65535;
note pkexpneg x -> exp(-x/256)*65536; pklog2q16 v -> log2(v)*65536; pkisqrt v; pkhash x y seed;
note pknoise x256 y256 seed; pkfbm x256 y256 seed octaves; pklenc light; pkscale c f; pkadd d c a;
note pkmix d c a; pksmooth t; pkeaseout t; pkprog now from upto; pkclip x y w h; pkglow cx cy r color a
note (16ths); pkthread x0 y0 x1 y1 color a01 (16ths, Pa as above); pksdrrect x y rx ry rw rh (Lg[9]);
note pkcover d16; pkletter pen y c color a plus -> pen after (pen in 1/256 px, plus true = additive).
const LOOKPX ulong 8294400
global Lg long 16
global Nfrm uint LOOKPX
global Nsky uint LOOKPX
global Slin ushort 256
global Ssrgb ushort 4096
global Pa long 8
global Psin long 4097
global Pexp ulong 4096
global Plog ulong 257
global Patan ulong 14
note Ps: 0 glow cx, 1 cy, 2 r2, 3 inv, 4 color, 5 a, 6 x0, 7 x1-1; 8..18 thread x0 y0 x1 y1 color a0 a1
note len grad radius steep yc, 27 a; 20..26 letter gx gy color a plus x0 x1; 28..31 pkfit x0 y0 x1 y1
global Ps long 32
global Pgc ulong 3
global Pgt ulong 514
